I think folks put too much importance on whether or not their artifact is
restricted.

If a monster doesn't care about silver and does care about shock, an unskilled
+7 Grayswandir is a few points of average damage worse than an expert
+7 Mjollnir.
If a monster does care about silver and doesn't care about shock, an unskilled
+7 Grayswandir averages 20 damage more than an expert +7 Mjollnir.

In other words, Grayswandir kicks so much ass that it doesn't matter if it's
unskilled; it's still about as good as any other weapon in the worst case, and
often is far far better.

I dislike Stormbringer as it's too easy to have accidents.
I dislike creating silly artifacts like Sting because it makes wishes for useful
artifacts like Grayswandir or the Master Key less fruitful.




